#!/bin/sh
exec timeout -k 10s 120s "$HOME/.local/bin/opencode-openclaw" run --auto --model opencode/longcat-2.5-preview-free --variant low --dir /workspace/antonina "ANTONINA-FRONTIER-REFILL. This is a dispatch-only pass whose sole purpose is to keep the Antonina mycelium broad and continuously populated. The Antonina board is the only queue and coordination authority. Use board author openclaw@marceline-dev. Read compact live-agent state first, then scan the open board queue from page 1 across all needed pages. A project/repository/workspace with any useful live agent is represented. While any actionable unrepresented project exists, launch at most one new front for each such project and keep scanning for another unrepresented project. NEVER add depth to a represented project in this refill pass. For each candidate, read its issue body and newest comment page before launch; if current state remains unclear, launch a bounded reconnaissance front rather than doing deep archaeology yourself. Respect fresh working claims and project-local policy. Do not list /workspace, inspect local BOARD artifacts, read old terminal-agent logs, inspect git history, harvest completed agents, integrate branches, or supervise existing workers in this pass. Those belong to the main orchestrator. Before launch append a working claim, reread for conflicts, launch detached with an explicit cwd, then append the real agent ID and worktree. Continue breadth until every actionable project discovered in this pass is represented or has a precise board-recorded blocker, then return immediately."
